#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124212 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/id #uuid "3344e23f-56eb-5880-b1cd-7198525daf91" :question/math-academy-id "e-12554" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\dfrac {x^2} {4} +  \\dfrac {y^2} 9  + z^2 = 1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the ellipsoid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} \\\\ z & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the interior of the ellipse $\\dfrac {x^2} {4} +  \\dfrac {y^2} 9 =  1$ and its boundary.  \n\nTherefore, the domain is of $z = z(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\bigg\\{ (x, y) \\,:\\, \\dfrac {x^2} {4} +  \\dfrac {y^2} 9 \\leq  1 \\bigg\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124311 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Intercepts of Spheres and Ellipsoids"}] :question/id #uuid "ca62112b-9989-5ede-9cbf-561f5dc2ba43" :question/math-academy-id "e-5263" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\dfrac {(x-2)^2} {2} +  {y^2} + \\dfrac{(z+1)^2}{2} =1,$ find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+(0)^{2}+\\frac{(0+1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =1,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $\\left(1, 0, 0\\right)$ and $\\left(3, 0, 0\\right).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124315 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Center and Radius of a Sphere"}] :question/id #uuid "8db4fc0c-416b-57a4-8612-a422a7681076" :question/math-academy-id "e-5311" :question/problem "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere $(x+1)^2 + y^2 + z^2 + 8z = 20?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a sphere centered at $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ with radius $r > 0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-x_0)^2 + (y-y_0)^2 + (z-z_0)^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $z$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+8z & =20 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+({z}^{2}+8z+16) & =20+16 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z+4)^{2} & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-(-1))^2 + (y-0)^2 + (z-(-4))^2 = 6^2,\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point $C(-1,0,-4)$ and the radius $r=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124316 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124507 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8db2909b-26fd-53bf-8ce2-9fca4451efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Traces of Ellipsoids"}] :question/id #uuid "ecc934f5-9339-5076-b2d0-58b113364b54" :question/math-academy-id "e-5312" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the sphere $x^2 + (y+2)^2 + (z-3)^2 = 25?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}+(0-3)^{2} & =25 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}+9 & =25 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of the circle of radius $4$ centered at $(0,-2)$ in the $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ac9957f-d872-5e8e-a7c0-667a268f52a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $2$ centered at $(0,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282207} {:answer/id #uuid "96019670-c53d-5489-90d0-be12c74ebdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $4$ centered at $(3,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282984} {:answer/id #uuid "b22e4617-2402-5d7c-a88e-6d70cc34ed7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at $(-3,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283233} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e12024-82d7-5a9d-882e-29f6c5d8dfc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at $(0,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283280} {:answer/id #uuid "e70dad21-1bd9-5644-8458-8d9ee21bded5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at $(0,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e70dad21-1bd9-5644-8458-8d9ee21bded5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at $(0,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283698} :answer-field/id #uuid "159e9d7d-82fa-5add-aa31-3a518efdac5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "329288e3-c4cc-54c9-9a15-597f2748e70c" :question/math-academy-id "q-164186" :question/problem "Given the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2,$ what is the domain of $z=z(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the sphere, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2} & =2 \\\\ (z-1)^{2} & =2-({x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}) \\\\ z-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{2-({x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2})} \\\\ z & =1\\pm \\sqrt{2-({x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-({x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2})\\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis inequality describes the interior and boundary of the circle \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2\n$$\n\nwhich is a circle of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at $(0,-3)$ in the $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Intercepts of Spheres and Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "deaaff1d-2f53-5526-b9ed-535630d5756b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,0,0)$ and $(0,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378901} {:answer/id #uuid "17f57ef3-1965-542a-8509-d666dc45f460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,0,0)$ and $(1,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378902} {:answer/id #uuid "9e676646-0856-570e-8bcd-d20224d8f963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(1,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378903} {:answer/id #uuid "a64da3c9-82ba-5665-ad69-2425dd422dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378904} {:answer/id #uuid "7c514f26-bc2a-5d32-8c20-7f9389b9ca6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c514f26-bc2a-5d32-8c20-7f9389b9ca6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378905} :answer-field/id #uuid "5335ca67-0549-5235-be81-8218ad9f5df2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9b1b1b70-34eb-5d7e-b7c6-825a90a4f8c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-164257" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{8}=1$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x+1 & =0 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solution $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercept with the $x$-axis is $(-1,0,0)$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Intercepts of Spheres and Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd89ecad-0fc0-5ba5-a620-05712d3a1b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-\\frac{1}{2},0)$ and $(0,1,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401448} {:answer/id #uuid "d50858b8-1fd8-5038-a72e-57fc3037d5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401449} {:answer/id #uuid "0fd95cab-9721-51ba-b9c4-0bf0be760265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-1,0)$ and $(0,1,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401450} {:answer/id #uuid "99d03f44-97f1-5754-9f11-086ea13d97fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-1,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401451} {:answer/id #uuid "4408e820-21f8-5788-8399-5558cbe467ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-\\frac{1}{2},0)$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fd95cab-9721-51ba-b9c4-0bf0be760265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-1,0)$ and $(0,1,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401450} :answer-field/id #uuid "de275abf-f996-5e86-903d-b371c046139e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "50783562-e3df-58d6-82c6-67c9daca87a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-164267" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{16}=1$, find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ y & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=-1$ and $y=1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-1,0)$ and $(0,1,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e27c7c5-b3d7-50cb-85b0-560d2fecc886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$  centered at  $(-2,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282094} {:answer/id #uuid "562279ec-aa68-57c5-97ab-4be6be6b32ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $5$  centered at  $(-2,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282420} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6619d0-5ea4-5680-b0d0-d4b3c881c63a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$  centered at  $(2,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282905} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f8c5ca-0f4a-58d4-8938-7bc71ccd4774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$  centered at  $(2,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283141} {:answer/id #uuid "b8754720-8501-55d4-8ad3-5644a69649e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $5$  centered at  $(-2,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c6619d0-5ea4-5680-b0d0-d4b3c881c63a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$  centered at  $(2,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282905} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7584b7a-6975-545e-acc3-6456d0d9a9f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23c592cc-cea2-59e9-87a3-1ede25e122f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-164310" :question/problem "Given the sphere $(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2}=5,$ what is the domain of $z=z(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the sphere, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =5 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =5-((x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}) \\\\ z & =\\pm \\sqrt{5-((x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-((x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2})\\ge 0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis inequality describes the interior and boundary of the circle \n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=5\n$$\n\nwhich is a circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $(2,-2)$ in the $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a6c225e-f491-5e05-b843-83e54051cfa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282057} {:answer/id #uuid "35448161-d255-514d-954c-5e929660ad6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282162} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce2afea-aa0f-500c-b847-6312c303ebba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282478} {:answer/id #uuid "6e4ebc5e-cde8-5528-8539-2771165cd827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282635} {:answer/id #uuid "9dee0856-787e-519c-9d62-8797aa0e1e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ce2afea-aa0f-500c-b847-6312c303ebba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282478} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa06a2cf-24bf-5313-8d0f-2029fa25bc49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "23a6cffd-2f3e-55b9-90d1-e96cd073fd8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-164408" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{3}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the ellipsoid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ (z+2)^{2} & =3(1-(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2}) \\\\ z+2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{3(1-(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2}\\ge 0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the interior of the circle $(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1$ and its boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is \n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Intercepts of Spheres and Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93617cf9-3d17-5af3-8b5b-0af3ff0a1366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2, 0, 0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121917} {:answer/id #uuid "a04ffbc6-9173-5b40-9429-59d068fa9e5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0, 0, 0)$ and $(4, 0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121918} {:answer/id #uuid "e2133937-5633-5d47-8538-ffd02df02013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-27, 0, 0)$ and $(27, 0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121919} {:answer/id #uuid "3545ce41-2bbd-57ae-ac23-25a5048e69a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-3\\sqrt{3}, 0, 0)$ and $(3\\sqrt{3}, 0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121920} {:answer/id #uuid "3ad1e2b2-723c-56e6-814e-f5a94e21b7f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2, 0, 0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121921}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fd32ea76-5111-5159-815d-d8b416fcdd3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121916} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee26a954-2923-5eeb-bf8b-2719bf513f99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402422} {:answer/id #uuid "e26ad3b1-ff38-5495-b616-e54f54399203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-3\\sqrt{3},0,0)$ and $(3\\sqrt{3},0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402423} {:answer/id #uuid "bc68d26e-96f7-5b4d-bdb5-b6fec5a2f084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402424} {:answer/id #uuid "a8fadca9-a9ca-555e-8dea-311a59bf25f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402425} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2d168a-5ddf-5432-87fc-13b24c45ff30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-27,0,0)$ and $(27,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8fadca9-a9ca-555e-8dea-311a59bf25f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402425} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf9fe7b8-269f-525e-b0db-d764b7345b0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "863f05c5-808b-57a4-8854-1d3c4552848f" :question/math-academy-id "q-35509" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{2}=1$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12}+\\frac{(0+1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $x=0$ and $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "082a32ce-b296-5003-96b1-005733688ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}<1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321210} {:answer/id #uuid "1e79ad55-c354-5085-a57d-b35a313f2df2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321380} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebb048b-9615-5f86-8bb2-d195a4e960db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}>1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321641} {:answer/id #uuid "d3ba424c-b946-5b84-99a3-ced6715ba531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322801} {:answer/id #uuid "e5d57852-8701-5303-9f7c-8c60bd4fdb2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e79ad55-c354-5085-a57d-b35a313f2df2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321380} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd3939ff-69de-5955-b8ca-889db4246765" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d6e03d2b-cbce-5eba-bc2e-8ab166e28ff2" :question/math-academy-id "q-35518" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+(z+2)^{2}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the ellipsoid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+(z+2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (z+2)^{2} & =1-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z+2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the interior of the ellipse $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1$ and its boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is \n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\le 1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124507 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8db2909b-26fd-53bf-8ce2-9fca4451efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Traces of Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1bd7de9-a700-53ba-bb74-824db7244231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $2\\sqrt{2}$ centered at $(2, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123867} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8ef26f-c072-55e1-85a0-ca7ef8e50ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $8$ centered at $(-2, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123868} {:answer/id #uuid "6acbff5a-0f5c-5ef6-955a-1d1d62897fd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $2\\sqrt{2}$ centered at $(-2, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123869} {:answer/id #uuid "6e025fca-9028-511a-945f-1f87be56f2f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $2$ centered at $(0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123870} {:answer/id #uuid "729742cd-31dc-5566-9b64-19f5f4f6b98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $8$ centered at $(0, 0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123871}] :answer-field/id #uuid "36a6ae45-d47e-5cb7-8c1d-a491e4962f42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123866}] :question/id #uuid "4f834611-40cb-5685-9ced-4292d1a87a6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70488" :question/problem "What is the projection of the intersection between the sphere $(x + 2)^{2} + y^{2} + z^{2} = 9$ and the plane $z = 1$ onto the $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Center and Radius of a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9d8e161-5ace-5fe6-8d6f-946c202107f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=3$ and $C(0,0,0).$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379870} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f854a5-0af1-58ab-b7aa-0d667ce09b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=3$ and $C(-2,0,0).$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379871} {:answer/id #uuid "fa53c021-67b3-5fcb-9aa0-da398494ee42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=3$ and $C(2,0,0).$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379872} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d95473-847c-5bc5-858d-15cf5e997f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=9$ and $C(2,0,0).$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379873} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d6829b-b972-5188-a54b-b480a892d2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=9$ and $C(-2,0,0).$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2f854a5-0af1-58ab-b7aa-0d667ce09b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=3$ and $C(-2,0,0).$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379871} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3b0594c-7106-573b-ae2e-fba27ccebf84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78363164-869e-5f95-8767-f9319085edc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-70561" :question/problem "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere $(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-(-2))^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}={3}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point point $C(-2,0,0)$ and the radius $r=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Center and Radius of a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f17f0fa-5554-5af1-8d20-82ce1eade1a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=2$ and $C(-2,3,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337185} {:answer/id #uuid "924177bd-a7c7-53cf-964d-23685b095f6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=2$ and $C(2,0,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337358} {:answer/id #uuid "96eabbe9-3cc4-5e24-b210-649fbae5d5d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=4$ and $C(-2,0,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337404} {:answer/id #uuid "be4a15a1-9ace-54f1-b832-3855f1ad7519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=2$ and $C(-2,0,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337722} {:answer/id #uuid "d03bcb2e-60f9-55dc-9d21-e05ecce02f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=4$ and $C(0,2,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be4a15a1-9ace-54f1-b832-3855f1ad7519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=2$ and $C(-2,0,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337722} :answer-field/id #uuid "edc78b35-c1cd-5923-ad36-fded8d5f5022" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "48405d9f-7a37-5f9c-8701-3161fdec2e3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-70648" :question/problem "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere $(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2}=4?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-(-2))^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2}={2}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point point $C(-2,0,3)$ and the radius $r=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Center and Radius of a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31387237-56d6-52c2-9715-e7aa1debedf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $C(0,5,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403372} {:answer/id #uuid "634baf73-26e0-5f65-be9f-a93d12600043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=10$ and $C(0,0,-5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403373} {:answer/id #uuid "7979aab2-f218-